- * dscam - camera test for the DSLinuxDSi desktop: a live preview of the DSi camera in a window, and photos.
+ * dscam - camera and photo viewer for the DSLinuxDSi desktop: a live preview of the DSi camera in a window, photos, and a viewer
+ * for the photos taken. One program on purpose: the 3D engine (which shows the picture) can only serve one program at a time.
  * The kernel (NDSFB_CAM_CMD / NDSFB_CAM_FRAME, see drivers/video/ndsfb.c) switches the camera on and delivers 256x192 RGB555 frames;
  * each frame is loaded as a texture and drawn on the 3D layer (dsgx.h), which is far faster than pushing pixels through Nano-X.
- * Keys: space, Enter or a tap in the window = photo (saved as /home/photos/photoNNN.bmp), c = the other camera, f = flip the
- * picture upside down, m = mirror it, b = swap red and blue (if the colours look wrong), q or Esc = quit.
- * The overlay text says what is going on, including the numbers from the set-up if it fails.
+ *   dscam           start with the live preview
+ *   dscam photos    start with the photo viewer (the Start menu's Photos). If dscam is already running, it is told to show the
+ *                   viewer (or the preview) and this one ends.
+ * Camera keys: space, Enter or a tap in the window = photo (saved as /home/photos/photoNNN.bmp), c = the other camera, f = flip the
+ * picture upside down, m = mirror it, b = swap red and blue (if the colours look wrong), v = the photo viewer, q or Esc = quit.
+ * Viewer keys: left/right (or , and . or a tap on the left/right third) = previous/next, d = delete (twice), v = back to the
+ * camera, q or Esc = quit. The camera is switched off (and its LED) while the viewer is shown.
  */
